## 🧠 REMINDER RULES PHILOSOPHY

This page answers **one calming question**:

> “Will the system remind my clients automatically, without embarrassing me?”

So:

* Human tone
* Predictable timing
* No complex logic

---

# 🧱 PAGE LAYOUT (DESKTOP)

```
┌──── Page Header ──────────────────────────┐
│ Reminder Rules                            │
│ Subtitle: Automatic follow-ups timeline  │
└───────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌──── Reminder Timeline (main) ─────────────┐
│ Before Due → Due Day → After Due          │
└───────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Think **timeline**, not form.

---

# 1️⃣ PAGE HEADER

### Title:

**Reminder Rules**

### Subtitle:

> “Automatically remind clients about pending payments”

No “Save” panic.
Changes auto-save.

---

# 2️⃣ REMINDER TIMELINE (CORE UI)

Vertical or horizontal timeline with cards.

### Default rules (pre-filled):

#### 🟡 Before Due

* **3 days before due**
* Channel: Email
* Tone: Polite

> “Just a gentle reminder that invoice #123 is due on…”

---

#### 🟠 Due Day

* **On due date**
* Channel: Email / WhatsApp
* Tone: Neutral

> “Invoice #123 is due today…”

---

#### 🔴 After Due

* **7 days overdue**
* Channel: WhatsApp
* Tone: Firm

> “Invoice #123 is overdue. Please confirm payment date.”

---

#### 🔥 Escalation (Optional MVP+)

* **15 days overdue**
* Channel: Manual reminder
* Message: “Please call client”

No auto-legal threats.

---

# 3️⃣ EACH RULE CARD CONTAINS

* Timing (editable dropdown)
* Channel (Email / WhatsApp)
* Message preview
* Enable / Disable toggle

No condition builders.
No AND / OR logic.

---

# 4️⃣ MESSAGE TEMPLATE EDITOR (SIMPLE)

Click “Edit message” →

* Plain text box
* Variables:

  * {{ClientName}}
  * {{InvoiceNumber}}
  * {{Amount}}
  * {{DueDate}}

Show preview below editor.

---

# 5️⃣ GLOBAL SETTINGS (BOTTOM)

Small section:

* Business signature
* Default sender email
* WhatsApp number (later)

---

# 6️⃣ EMPTY / FIRST-TIME STATE

If no rules exist:

> “We’ve added default reminder rules for you.
> You can customize them anytime.”

This reduces fear.

---

# ❌ WHAT NOT TO ADD

* Cron expressions
* Workflow builders
* Legal language templates
* Multiple branches
* AI-generated messages (yet)

Keep it human.

---

# 🎨 VISUAL STYLE

* Soft cards
* Calm colors
* No red warnings
* Toggle switches, not checkboxes

This page should feel **safe**.

---

# 🧠 WHY THIS PAGE BUILDS TRUST

* Users fear annoying clients
* You give control without complexity
* Automation feels respectful

That’s rare.

---

# 📱 MOBILE BEHAVIOR

* Vertical timeline
* Expandable cards
* Inline editing

